Proposal (lane RELEASE, N5 and grill Q15): retire every automated review workflow.

Not applied: .github/ and tools/ are frozen; only Lucas applies this, by his hand or
his word. Apply from the repository root:

    git apply --check tools/release/proposals/retire-review-workflows.patch
    git apply --index tools/release/proposals/retire-review-workflows.patch

Lucas, grill Q15 (CONTRACT 1521-1523): "Let's retire all checks and have the gates
reported by me, since I own the subscriptions I can use the other models to review
and work intensively". CONTRACT 1525-1528: "No automated review check will run on any
repository"; "Recursion's Codex gate and Claude fixer workflows retire. The new core's
CI runs tests and no review check". The Liaison's ruling of 4:20 PM, Nov 14, 2026 puts
every automated review entry point in this patch, stuck-thread-watch.yml included.

Removed:
- .github/workflows/codex-gate.yml, claude.yml, claude-conflict-writer.yml,
  conflict-scan.yml (it exists to call the conflict writer) and stuck-thread-watch.yml
  (the Codex mediator: on a schedule and on comments and reviews it posts `@codex
  review` on stuck review threads with a personal token, replies there, resolves
  threads and takes in the Claude fixer's failures);
- .github/actionlint.yaml (its only entries are four of those files);
- the scripts only those workflows run: .github/scripts/stuck_thread_watch.py,
  scripts/ci/codex_gate.py, claude_conflict_scan.py, claude_denials.py,
  claude_pr_fixer_gate.py, fixer_failure_escalation.py, install_pinned_claude_code.sh
  and the Claude Code pin and signing fingerprint;
- the tests that exist only for them: tools/test_claude_pr_fixer.py,
  tools/test_codex_gate.py, tools/test_codex_gate_identity.py,
  tools/test_stuck_thread_watch.py, tools/test_fixer_failure_watcher.py,
  tools/test_fixer_failure_escalation.py.
Edited so the gate stays green:
- tools/ci_gate.py: TEST_EXCLUDE held only tools/test_claude_pr_fixer.py;
- .claude/settings.json: the allow rules of the six removed tests (the settings guard
  derives the expected rules from tools/test_*.py);
- tools/test_ci_scheduling.py: the writer admission guard becomes a guard that no
  workflow runs review automation (the Claude Code action or its credentials,
  `@codex review`, the mediator's token or script, the Codex gate) and that the five
  files stay gone;
- tools/test_claude_fixer_guard.py and tools/test_claude_fixer_publish.py: kept,
  because CSL-495 (Lucas, Oct 26) keeps tools/test_claude_fixer_* and the X1
  inventory test pins them; only their tests of the retired workflows' wiring go.
  The publisher test keeps its standard-library workflow loader and WorkflowYamlTests,
  which still read every surviving workflow.
Kept on purpose: scripts/ci/claude_fixer_guard.py, claude_fixer_publish.py,
claude_fixer_outbox.py and claude_fixer_receipts.py, which the CSL-495 tests test.
Not edited (documents that still name the retired workflows): AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md,
README.md, docs/ci-event-contract.md, .claude/skills/proceed-or-escalate/SKILL.md.
The Devin Review app check on pull requests is an app install, not a workflow; only an
owner can remove it.

Blank context lines are written as empty lines, which git apply accepts; the file
then has no trailing whitespace for the gate's whitespace check.

